# Prebuilt omni-stt images that setup.sh may deploy instead of building one in
# your project. KEY=value lines only: setup.sh reads this file, it never runs it.
#
# OMNI_STT_IMAGE: the stock omni-stt image (Omnilingual 300M card, VoxLingua107
# language ID, Silero VAD, the Haitian Creole voices), on GitHub Container
# Registry and pinned by digest:
#   OMNI_STT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/lithsec/omni-stt@sha256:<64 hex digits>
# setup.sh pulls it through an Artifact Registry remote repository in your
# project (named "ghcr", upstream https://ghcr.io), so Cloud Run deploys
#   <region>-docker.pkg.dev/<your project>/ghcr/lithsec/omni-stt@sha256:<digest>
# Only stock weights may be published there, never a fine-tuned card, and no
# layer may be over 9.9 GB (Cloud Run's limit for images from an external
# registry, remote repositories included).
#
# Built and published by .github/workflows/omni-stt-image.yml (tag omni-stt-<date>
# or a manual run), which checks the layer sizes before it pushes; provenance:
#   gh attestation verify oci://ghcr.io/lithsec/omni-stt@<digest> --repo lithsec/translation-open-stack
# 2026.10.28: 16.6 GB unpacked. Largest layers, unpacked / compressed: PyTorch and
# its CUDA libraries 7.8 / 4.3 GB, the models (300M checkpoint 6.1 GB, language ID
# and voices 1.2 GB) 7.8 / 7.2 GB.
# Empty: setup.sh builds the image in your project instead, with Cloud Build.
OMNI_STT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/lithsec/omni-stt@sha256:7741609ab365bf2e72ca1f541951debdc0fc8d5437a6a102e540c04959bf642e

# The 7B service (Lao and Khmer) is always built in your project: its checkpoint
# is one 15.6 GB file, a single layer over the 9.9 GB limit above, so it cannot
# come through a remote repository. setup.sh builds it with Cloud Build
# (deploy.sh 7b-build: Meta's stock checkpoint, converted to bf16) into a
# standard Artifact Registry repository, which takes large layers.
